' 4+1 logical view - States of an owner (D-USER with the Owner profile) · users.deactivated_at
' Version 1.1 - 2026-11-10
' For: whoever writes the code.
' Documented decision: Deactivating an owner is a conditional UPDATE of users.deactivated_at, with an append-only history (US29).
' Not drawn: controllers, HTTP and screens.
@startuml logical-state-owner
!include ../style.puml
title Logical view - states of an owner (account with the Owner profile): users.deactivated_at

hide empty description
state Active : deactivated_at empty
state Deactivated : deactivated_at set\nno login or refresh\nclubs hidden, no new bookings

[*] --> Active : AccountRegistrationService.RegisterOwnerAsync\n(or seed-demo)
Active --> Deactivated : AdminOwnerStatusService.DeactivateAsync\n→ IOwnerStatusStore.TryChangeAsync(Deactivated)\nUPDATE … WHERE deactivated_at IS NULL\n+ row in owner_status_changes\n+ revokes the owner's refresh tokens
Deactivated --> Active : AdminOwnerStatusService.ReactivateAsync\n→ TryChangeAsync(Reactivated)\nUPDATE … WHERE deactivated_at IS NOT NULL\n+ row in owner_status_changes
Active --> Active : reactivate → 422 owner_not_deactivated
Deactivated --> Deactivated : deactivate → 422 owner_already_deactivated

note right of Deactivated
  All in one transaction; the conditional UPDATE decides
  (0 rows = already in that state, nothing is written).
  No booking is cancelled. The access token already
  issued lasts up to 15 min (accepted).
end note

@enduml
